--- task
id: r01
dataset: reading
kind: lexical ranking with the score
answer: fewest

--- intent
Rank the documents by how relevant their body is to the text `$q` (BM25) and return the top 3 slugs with the score as `score`, best first.

--- params
{"q": "needle"}

--- edition2
query relevant($q: String) {
  match { $d: Doc }
  return { $d.slug, bm25($d.body, $q) as score }
  order { bm25($d.body, $q) desc }
  limit 3
}

--- edition3 disputed
query relevant($q: String) {
  match { from bm25({ match { $d: Doc } return { $d } }, $d.body, $q) as $score }
  return { $d.slug, $score }
  order { $score desc }
  limit 3
}

--- edition3 disputed
query relevant($q: String) {
  match { from bm25({ match { $d: Doc } return { $d } }, $d.body, $q) as $score }
  return { $d.slug, $score as score }
  order { $score desc }
  limit 3
}

--- expect ordered
columns: ["d.slug","score"]
["d0",0.7411202]
["d3",0.71866196]
["d1",0.65877354]

--- note
Disputed on #1316 at a1b89621 (the 2026-11-19 M0 re-run): the edition-3 text is accepted and returns the recorded documents in the recorded order, but `bm25` scores are F64 there while the rows recorded from edition 2 hold F32 scores (2.0232521362860822 against 2.0232522), so its rows differ from the recorded rows by value. The rows are not edited; the text is kept as `edition3 disputed`, not a truth.
